-- Native sigils and a char pin (s55), ASCII twin: a kanji ^alias narrows to the marked rows, a :Sym matches and then writes kanji symbol values, and the kanji char column is pinned directly — sym values and char columns become writable and pinnable in kanji.
-- The sigils go native too: ^照準 is an alias, :勇者 a symbol value, and the pin reads the glyph column back exactly.
--! registry ../registries/s55-native-sigils.reg
--! expect 印 = .#..#.
--! expect 打撃 = 0 0 0 0 0 9
--! expect 派閥 = 山賊 勇者 山賊 勇者 山賊 賊軍

^照準 & 派閥 == :勇者 , 打撃 = 9 ; 派閥 = :賊軍
